<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26795" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Līris</span></b> , is, m.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a river between
				Latium and Campania</i>, now <i>Garigliano</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Hor.
				C. 1, 31, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 4, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 103, 106, § 227, 3, 5,
				9, § 56</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Leg. 2,
				3, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 2, 424</span></i>.— <i>Acc.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lirem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Leg. 2, 3, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lirim,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					26, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lirin,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 12, 56</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Līrī-nas</span></b>  or
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Līrēnas</span></b> , ātis,
				<i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to
				the Liris</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">interamnates Succasini, qui et Lirenates
					vocantur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					3, 5, 9, § 54</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
